.SS "int meta_dflt (noir_md * a, meta_flags flags, meta_type type, const char * k, const char * d, const char * g, const char * v, noir_provider * p)"
.PP
set a default for a meta-data entry: \fBmeta_add()\fP only if value does not already exist. 
.PP
sometimes, a meta-data entry must be created even if it is not warranted by the file we wish to describe. for instance, if no 'genre' information is set on a MP3 song, we will still want to create a 'genre'-entry in the meta-data so the info-dialog will create a 'genre' edit-field. to do this, the provider's \fBmeta_get_for_file()\fP function should first create entries for all meta-data it can get from the file, and then call \fBmeta_dflt()\fP for all items that an entry must exist for 'no matter what.'
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
an error-code 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP - the list 
.br
\fIflags\fP - the flags for the entry (read-only etc.) 
.br
\fItype\fP - the type of the entry (integer, UTF8, ...) 
.br
\fIk\fP - the name of the entry 
.br
\fId\fP - the description for the entry, or NULL 
.br
\fIg\fP - the group the entry should appear in 
.br
\fIv\fP - the value for the entry, or NULL 
.br
\fIp\fP - the provider that created the entry
.RE
.PP

